// Renovate, for this repository.
//
// Everything general - when updates arrive, what groups with what, what may
// merge itself, and since 2026-09-16 how the family's own packages and the
// toolchain are handled - lives in Lautstark/.github and is true of every
// repository. What is here is the part that is true of this one and would be
// wrong to inherit.
//
// The .json5 is spelled out on purpose: the //path/to/file syntax implies a
// .json extension, so omitting it looks for a file that is not there and
// Renovate stops before it does anything. The shorter "owner/repo:name" form
// implies it too.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: ["github>Lautstark/.github//renovate-shared.json5"],

  packageRules: [
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    // The shared packages: what "a bump is a decision" means since 2026-09-16
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------------
    //
    // Until that date this file disabled Renovate for @lautstark/** outright:
    // the packages were github: tags, thought hard for the npm manager to
    // follow (it is not: a github:owner/repo#vX.Y.Z pin resolves through the
    // github-tags datasource), and
    // a bump of one was a decision rather than an update - made by a person
    // moving the pin, with pins.js saying when one had fallen behind.
    //
    // The packages are tagged from their main branches by CI now - there is
    // still no registry, and the pin is still a github: tag, which Renovate
    // follows through the github-tags datasource - and the decision has not
    // gone away; it has moved to where the information is. The package's author makes it in the commit subject -
    // feat is a minor, fix a patch, feat! a major - and this repository's
    // tests make it again on the branch Renovate pushes. So the shared preset
    // says: a minor or a patch of a shared package merges to main on its own
    // once the tests here are green, and a major waits for a person with the
    // changelog in front of them. That rule is not repeated here.
    //
    // This repository takes one shared package, @lautstark/design, and it
    // follows the preset. Nothing to except - the rule is written for the
    // namespace there, so which packages this repository depends on can
    // change without this file noticing.
  ],
}
